### Method reminder

Link the characteristic (age) to the reasons for migrating (jobs, education, freedom to move).

### Solution

Young adults, roughly 15 to 35 years old, dominate migration.

Reasons (any two):
- they are looking for work, training or higher education that is not available at home;
- they are physically fit and able to bear the cost and risks of the journey;
- they have fewer family ties (children, property) than older people and more years ahead to profit from the move;
- children depend on their parents and the old have little chance of finding work at the destination.
